# /etc/ebooktrivia/walg.env (0640 root:<app user>): wal-g in the PostgreSQL container (US-015, docs/runbooks/backups.md): the archive command
# of every WAL segment (RPO about a minute) and the nightly base backup (infra/backup/walg-base-backup.sh), encrypted client-side with
# libsodium, to S3-compatible storage. The location is the operator's: host-check.sh fails while __SET_ME__ is left.
#   WALG_S3_PREFIX   s3://<bucket>/<path>, for example s3://ebt-staging-pitr/walg
#   AWS_ENDPOINT     the provider's S3 endpoint URL (https), for example https://s3.eu-central-1.example.com
#   AWS_REGION       its region name
# The libsodium key and the S3 credentials are NOT here but FILES in /etc/ebooktrivia/postgres (mounted read-only into the container,
# never environment): walg_libsodium.key (generated by provision.sh, once: escrow it the day it is made, docs/escrow.md) and
# walg_aws_credentials (an AWS shared-credentials file the operator fills in). Do not change the key afterwards: backups made with
# one key cannot be read with another.
WALG_S3_PREFIX=__SET_ME__
AWS_ENDPOINT=__SET_ME__
AWS_REGION=__SET_ME__
AWS_S3_FORCE_PATH_STYLE=true
AWS_SHARED_CREDENTIALS_FILE=/etc/walg/aws-credentials
WALG_LIBSODIUM_KEY_PATH=/etc/walg/libsodium.key
WALG_LIBSODIUM_KEY_TRANSFORM=hex
WALG_COMPRESSION_METHOD=zstd
